<title>USA: Bethlehem Steel takes Florida building stake.</title>
<headline>Bethlehem Steel takes Florida building stake.</headline>
<dateline>ORLANDO, Fla. 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bethlehem Steel Corp said Friday it formed a venture with CSR Rinker, the largest building materials company in Florida, to expand the use of steel in residential and light commercial building construction.</p>
<p>Under the terms of the agreement, Bethlehem Steel will purchase 45 percent of Steel Construction Systems, a CSR Rinker subsidiary, for undisclosed terms. The venture will continue to be known as Steel Construction Systems.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.))</p>
</text>
